              "compound_details": "THIS IS THE STRUCTURE OF THE MANDELATE RACEMASE MUTANT\nLYSINE 166 -> ARGININE CO-CRYSTALLIZED WITH THE SUBSTRATE\n(R)-MANDELIC ACID.  THE SUBSTRATE THAT IS BOUND AT THE\nACTIVE SITE IS RESIDUE 399 FOR CONSISTENCY WITH THE\nNOMENCLATURE OF PREVIOUS MANDELATE RACEMASE STRUCTURES.\nIT HAS THE RESIDUE NAME SMN BECAUSE IT IS THE (S)-ISOMER.\nTHE (S)-ENANTIOMER PRESUMABLY AROSE FROM THE SLOW\nRACEMIZATION OF (R)-MANDELATE.  THERE IS A SECOND SUBSTRATE\nMOLECULE IN THE STRUCTURE; IT IS LOCATED IN THE REGION\nLEADING TO THE ACTIVE SITE.  THIS MOLECULE IS THE\n(R)-STEREOISOMER.  IT IS RESIDUE 398 AND, BY ANALOGY, HAS\nTHE RESIDUE NAME RMN.",
